			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Remove stale .commit-message.json artifact\n\nThe `.commit-message.json` file at the Mountain root was left behind from the commit message generation workflow and contains the message text of the most recent commit (3e14d7e8). This file has no purpose outside the generation pipeline and should not be tracked.\n\nUnstage and delete the artifact.",
			"SHA": "b991e9aa7f464743fe1aa8efc9d545504871e0cf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:23:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Bridge WebSocket frames to MountainIPCInvoke dispatch\n\nRegister a default handler on the Mist handler registry that bridges every\ninbound `{ method, params }` WebSocket frame into the\n`crate::IPC::WindServiceHandlers::mountain_ipc_invoke` dispatch path — the\nsame Tauri command used by the Sky frontend — so the full\nWindServiceHandlers surface is reachable over the Mist WebSocket transport\nwithout per-method registration.\n\nThe handler normalises params into a Vec<Value> (Array passes through,\nNull becomes empty, scalars wrap into single-element) and delegates to the\nexisting mountain_ipc_invoke. The Mist secret is wrapped in Some() for\nconsistent optional semantics on ServeLocal.\n\nThis eliminates the staged handler-registration plan described in the\nprevious comment: the fallback makes every method available immediately.",
			"SHA": "3e14d7e8b3d31fb0c80ff943a64015d2d7d3f3d0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:22:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add CancelOnDrop guard to provider forward calls\n\nReplace the direct `IPCProvider::SendRequestToSideCar` in `InvokeProvider`\nand `InvokeProviderMethod` with `ForwardCancellable`, a wrapper that runs\nthe Vine call on a detached `tokio::spawn` task guarded by a drop-triggered\nwatch signal. A new `CancelOnDrop` guard flips the signal when the calling\nfuture is dropped — from gRPC cancellation, typed-rail `CancelOperation`,\npeer disconnect, or any caller-side `select!` loss — so the detached task\ndelivers `CocoonService.CancelOperation` for the wire request id before\nexiting, terminating the side-car provider instead of computing a result\nnobody is waiting for.\n\nBoth provider-invocation paths now use `FnCancellable` from the Vine\nclient instead of the old blocking `SendRequestToSideCar`, eliminating\nthe `Arc<dyn IPCProvider>` / `Require()` dependency in both modules.",
			"SHA": "c1eb47dc38cbaf90ea0132444cba790bf24f046b"
		}
	],
